special_abilities:
  - name: "Master of Internal Energy"
    description: "The chi-gung pouring out of the monk must be meant for something, and the Seng Ren goes looking for what: it explores and tests the power wherever it can be used, goes where people suffer most because healing seems its best use, and seeks out other champions who fight evil."
  - name: "Trained to Sense and Manipulate Chi"
    description: "Taught to gather and direct chi, the life force that exists even in very weak P.P.E. environments. This is the basis of every Chi-Gung power."
  - name: "Chi-Gung Powers"
    description: "Self-discovered rather than taught in a school. Six picked at level 1 from the 29 Chi-Gung powers (printed 56-62), and two more at each level after. Limits of Chi-Gung: one power at a time, and the active one must be cancelled (at will) or run out before another is used, with a rare few exceptions; most Chi-Gung powers can only be used by the Seng Ren; all cost I.S.P. to activate and many cost more every melee round to keep working. The monk never gains psionic powers other than those that apply to chi-gung."
  - name: "Super I.S.P. Regeneration"
    description: "Recovers 5 I.S.P. per melee round at levels one and two, 10 I.S.P. per melee round at levels 3 and 4, and 15 I.S.P. per melee round from 5th level on. The permanent pool is modest for a master psychic; the rate at which it refills is what sets the Seng Ren apart."
  - name: "Powers of Meditation"
    description: "From an early age the character has focused all inner strength into meditation, contemplation and sensitivity to the stirring of chi."
