extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 25: China 2 printed 54-62 (cache p055-p063, scan, page_offset +1), read off 200 dpi renders: the class on printed 54-56, its 29 Chi-Gung power descriptions on printed 56-62, ending where Chinese Diviners begins on printed 62. The section heading is Mystic Monks (printed 52), so occ_group is psychic per the China 2 brief; the class states its own S.D.C. (3D6+36), so no men_of_arms line. The book subtitles it Monk of Internal Energy, also known as the Chi-Gung Energy Master. XP ladder: printed 160 (cache p161), the block headed Enlightened Demon / Monk: Chi-Gung Sen Ren / Warrior: Nei Chia Wu Shih, read off a render. Psionics: printed 55 calls it a Master Psychic saving vs psionic attack on 10 or higher, so type master. I.S.P. base M.E. +5D10, +5 per level. The powers are the 29 Chi-Gung rows (psionic_powers, category Special), named in powers_from: six at level 1 and two more at every level after (printed 55). Super I.S.P. Regeneration (5/10/15 per melee round by level) is prose. Hand to hand: one of five China styles is picked; the book prints no other style and no price, so none is sold (hand_to_hand costs {}). O.C.C. bonuses (printed 55): +1D4+3 M.E. and +1D4 M.A. (dice, rolled at creation), +2 save vs possession, +3 vs Demonic Curses (curses), +2 save vs magic at levels 1, 3, 7, 10 and 14 (spell_magic only; read as +2 at each listed level), +1 initiative at levels 4, 8 and 12, +1 save vs Horror Factor at levels 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15. Skills: Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic; the book''s Lore: Ancient & Classical Chinese is the Literacy row; Language: Native Chinese Speaker (95%) is Language: Native Tongue at 95; Literacy: Chinese at 75 keeps the catalog''s +5 per level. W.P. lists: Battle Axe is W.P. Axe, Large Sword and Small Sword are both W.P. Sword, Spear (Throwing) is W.P. Spear. Related skills: several categories are none at first level but any thereafter, and Rogue is limited to Calligraphic Forgery (+5%), Concealment and Dickering at first level; nothing gates a category by level, so those categories are granted whole and the first-level limits are in the note (the +5% to Calligraphic Forgery is in the note only). W.P. Heavy Weapons and Heavy Energy Weapons are read as W.P. Heavy Military Weapons and W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons. Equipment: identification documents with a monastery passport and letters of recommendation, a collection of herbs, two sets of chopsticks and 10 cups of uncooked rice have no catalog row and are in the Lore; the warm cloak is hooded-cloak and the begging bowl bowl-earthenware."
